WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.898
Advanced format features create risk when they are enabled without a
matching need.

2
00:00:04.898 --> 00:00:11.727
YAML can support tags, anchors, aliases, references, metadata, and
application-specific construction behavior.

3
00:00:11.727 --> 00:00:18.280
XML can involve parser configuration, schemas, namespaces, entity
handling, and external resource behavior.

4
00:00:18.280 --> 00:00:24.972
These features may be useful in controlled systems, but they should not be
accepted casually from untrusted input.

5
00:00:24.972 --> 00:00:31.663
YAML safe loader concepts are about loading ordinary data rather than
broadly constructing application objects.

6
00:00:31.663 --> 00:00:38.492
For untrusted or lightly trusted YAML, the parser should accept a simple
and predictable subset whenever practical.

7
00:00:38.492 --> 00:00:47.460
Configuration files and user-submitted YAML should not receive the same
authority unless the source, review process, and intended behavior justify
it.

8
00:00:47.460 --> 00:00:51.116
XML parser settings can influence security and availability.

9
00:00:51.116 --> 00:01:00.567
External resource access, entity handling, expansion behavior, validation
mode, namespace processing, and resource limits all deserve review at a
high level.

10
00:01:00.567 --> 00:01:03.947
The defensive goal is not to memorize every parser option.

11
00:01:03.947 --> 00:01:10.501
The goal is to choose parser behavior deliberately, disable unnecessary
features, and constrain resource use.

12
00:01:10.501 --> 00:01:13.260
Flexible formats need explicit expectations.

13
00:01:13.260 --> 00:01:20.089
If tags, aliases, external references, schema features, or metadata are
not required, do not enable them by default.

14
00:01:20.089 --> 00:01:27.608
If they are required, document the reason, validate the structure, bound
resource use, and test unsupported or malformed cases.

15
00:01:27.608 --> 00:01:32.920
Advanced features should be treated as design decisions, not incidental
parser defaults.
